1
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:13,100
A plan Claude Code executed on its own. Nineteen nodes. One evening.

2
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:25,100
Felix Rieseberg's method: altitude, depth, range.

3
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:37,100
A node is not done because the model says so. It needs a proof. Only I can validate.

4
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:47,600
Three agents, three branches, one benchmark.

5
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:58,600
Then I ran the benchmark myself. 334 ms down to 44.

6
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:11,600
Cost and time on screen before and during. Estimates calibrated against real timings.

7
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:24,600
After each turn, the plugin hands Claude the next open node.

8
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:33,600
And I steer from anywhere. Validate, go deeper, go wider, prune.

9
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:42,500
Ambiflex. Open source, one line to install.
